    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Once alligation gives a ratio, turn ratio-parts into real quantity.\n\nSuppose cheaper : dearer = 3:2 and the total mixture is 40 kg.\n\nThere are 5 equal parts.\nOne part = 40 ÷ 5 = 8 kg.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So the quantities are:\ncheaper = 3×8 = 24 kg\ndearer = 2×8 = 16 kg.\n\nAlways split the total by total ratio-parts first. That keeps the arithmetic small.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
