    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Capstone: price gaps give the ratio, then the ratio gives quantity.\n\nSuppose ₹42 and ₹54 ingredients must make ₹48.\n\nAlligation gives:\n(54−48):(48−42) = 6:6 = 1:1.\n\nFor 30 kg total, that means 15 kg of each.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The full mental chain is:\n1. Check the mean lies between the two values.\n2. Cross the gaps to get the ratio.\n3. Convert ratio-parts to quantity.\n4. Recheck the weighted mean.\n\nThat four-step check is more reliable than memorising a diagram.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
